New members can register, sign up, and log into FingerMobile right now.

The entire registration and onboarding lifecycle was tested end-to-end against the active PostgreSQL database (fingermobile_platform_db on port 5433) and live API (http://localhost:5001).

What Happens Automatically When a New Member Registers:
Persistent Account Creation in PostgreSQL:
The user record is inserted directly into the users table with bcrypt-hashed credentials (salt rounds = 12), sovereign username, email, phone, and assigned Member role.

Automated Profile Initialization:
Both member_profiles and user_profile tables are automatically provisioned and linked via foreign key to the new user ID.
Automated Wallet & Vault Provisioning:
Both fic_wallets and enhanced_wallets are automatically created for the member with a 5.00 FIC initial platform welcome balance. This 5.00 FIC is the signup fee for the platform. This is what will be deducted from the member's wallet upon successful registration. 

Instant Verification & Session Tokens:
Cryptographic JWT accessToken, refreshToken, and session cookies are generated.
In development mode (autoVerify: true), the member is verified immediately so they can transition straight to the dashboard or start participating in Forums, Gems, Groups, and Marketplaces without email waiting friction.
Full Cascade & Soft-Delete Safe:
Database storage quota triggers (calculate_user_storage()) handle account creation, updates, and soft-deletes with zero foreign key violations.

